title: 'First end-to-end lifecycle verification: a real KNOT on a fresh repo, and two instruments that were lying'
summary: 'Ran the never-started dress rehearsal on a genuinely fresh repo ahead of the first field test (an Expo/React Native app). The full native cycle — genesis, fork x2, propose x2, FAST_ADMIT, KNOT with hydrated payload, human resolve, backup, destroy, byte-identical restore — passed, producing the first GENUINE KNOT this project has ever made. The run exposed that 55.9% of the WORKTREE-absorbed symbol universe was Swift build output with machine-absolute paths in the ids, and that `warpline health` was structurally blind to every KNOT the native path produces. CORRECTION (post-hoc, founder-prompted): the sealed LEDGER was never polluted — seals absorb a git ref via `git archive`, which carries git-tracked files only, so the junk never entered history and there is NO mass-retirement to seal. The claimed "~16,015 symbols retiring" was wrong; the measured seal delta was +2.'
