body: |-
  CONTEXT. Resumed from a checkpoint into a founder directive: be completely ready for the first true field test, which will be a completely fresh repo. That reframing is what made the dress rehearsal the priority — a fresh repo IS the rehearsal, and the rehearsal had never been started.

  THE FIELD TEST TARGET. Confirmed with the founder mid-session: an iOS/Android app that "probably doesn't need to be native Swift" — i.e. React Native / Expo, which is TypeScript. This is the good outcome: the TS lens covers the app code on day one. Flutter/Dart or Kotlin Multiplatform would have needed a new lens before the test could measure anything, since Warpline's entire semantic universe is TS/TSX code units + JSON/YAML config units + .purpose files.

  It also sharpened the lens fix from "nice" to "blocking": an Expo app ships ios/Pods/, android/build/, android/.gradle/ and .expo/, all dense with JSON/plist, none of them in either lens's old skip-list. Without the fix the .build explosion would have reproduced on day one of the field test. Expo's default .gitignore covers all of them at ROOT level, so honoring root ignore files is sufficient — no nested-gitignore work needed for the test.

  WHAT THE REHEARSAL PROVED. On a fresh `git init` repo with no .purpose files, git absent for the whole native cycle: absorb produced 5 sensible symbols (1 TS code unit + 4 config units); genesis sealed; two agents forked the SAME selvage; both edited the same function and proposed with claims; A fast-admitted; B produced a KNOT (exit 1) naming the contested unit with base/ours/theirs essences, blast radius, and the untrusted-prose envelope intact around agent-authored intent; the human resolve leg sealed decidedBy/reason/contended and advanced the selvage; backup created and verified (35 files digest-true, 4 strands authenticated); the entire .warpline was destroyed; restore from the backup root reproduced the worktree BYTE-IDENTICAL.

  Per FG-1 (agent-class F4 completion = reaches KNOT + hydrates knotPayloadId), that is the completion condition met on the path the field test will use.

  A LEGIBILITY DATA POINT WORTH KEEPING. It took several wrong attempts to drive the cycle even with the source open. `admit --native` returned NOOP three times because the agent's work must first be SEALED by `propose --native`, and `warpline propose --help` describes only the claim side-effect — it never says that this is the verb that captures your work. `--worktree` on admit governs only the CLEAN write-back, not what gets absorbed. A cold agent reading only --help would not find this path. That is direct evidence for the F4 cold-agent legibility constraint (TD-2026-07-21-766) and argues for a propose/admit help rewrite before the field test.

  NOT DONE, DELIBERATELY. The one-time correction seal on this repo (~16,015 symbols retiring) has not been made — it should be an intent-labelled, founder-visible pick rather than something the auto-seal hook does silently on the next commit. The 30-50 seal scale run to see the cost curve has not been done. The counterfactual denominator on this repo is still 1 of 44.
